{
  "title": "Ulnar Tunnel Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6022/ulnar-tunnel-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 2 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Ulnar Tunnel Syndrome is a compressive neuropathy of the ulnar nerve at the level of the wrist (Guyon's canal), most commonly due to a ganglion cyst.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made clinically with paresthesias of the small and ring finger with intrinsic weakness with a Tinel's sign over Guyon's canal.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment involves a course of conservative management with splinting, and surgical decompression in the presence of a compressive lesion (i.e ganglion) or continued symptoms.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "less common than cubital tunnel syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "cyclists (also known as handlebar palsy)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "causes of compression include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**ganglion cyst (**80% of nontraumatic causes)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**lipoma**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**repetitive trauma**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**ulnar artery thrombosis or aneurysm**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**hook of hamate fracture or nonunion**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**pisiform dislocation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**inflammatory arthritis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**fibrous band, muscle or bony anomaly**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**congenital bands**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**palmaris brevis hypertrophy**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**idiopathic**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Guyon’s canal",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "course",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "is approximately 4 cm long",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "begins at the proximal extent of the transverse carpal ligament and ends at the aponeurotic arch of the hypothenar muscles",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "contents",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ulnar nerve bifurcates into the superficial sensory and deep motor branches",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "boundaries and zones (see table below)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
